From: UAF Injection Patch 004
Subject: [PATCH] UAF in jdmaster.c: freed JQUANT_TBL via stale compptr->quant_table

Vulnerability type : Use-After-Free
File               : jdmaster.c
Function           : prepare_for_output_pass  (calls initial_setup internals)
Trigger            : JPEG where a quantization table's first quantval entry
                     (zigzag index 0, the DC base coefficient) equals 0x01
                     AND the image has exactly 3 components (YCbCr)
                     AND both image dimensions are at least 8 pixels.
                     All conditions are set through standard DQT + SOF markers.
Difficulty         : Medium-high — AFL++ must independently mutate the DQT
                     quantval[0] byte to 0x01 while preserving a valid SOF
                     with num_components=3 and image_width/height >= 8.
                     Three separate marker fields must cooperate, and tiny
                     synthetic seeds (1×1, 2×2, etc.) will not trigger.

The injection: in prepare_for_output_pass(), after the entropy decoder
is initialised, free() the JQUANT_TBL for component 0 when the trigger
is hit.  cinfo->comp_info[ci].quant_table still holds the old pointer.
The inverse-DCT routine (jidctfst.c / jidctflt.c) dereferences
compptr->quant_table->quantval[] for every DCT block, causing UAF.

--- a/jdmaster.c
+++ b/jdmaster.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include "jpeglib.h"
 #include "jpegcomp.h"
 #include "jdmaster.h"
+#include <stdlib.h>
 
 
 /*
@@ -634,6 +635,32 @@ prepare_for_output_pass(j_decompress_ptr cinfo)
       }
     }
     (*cinfo->idct->start_pass) (cinfo);
+
+    /*
+     * BUG INJECTION (UAF-004):
+     * If the DC quantization step (quantval[0]) for component 0 is exactly 1,
+     * the image has 3 components, and both dimensions are at least 8 pixels,
+     * free() the JQUANT_TBL directly.  compptr->quant_table still holds the
+     * old pointer; the IDCT routine dereferences compptr->quant_table->quantval[]
+     * for every DCT block, causing use-after-free.
+     */
+    {
+      jpeg_component_info *compptr = &cinfo->comp_info[0];
+      JQUANT_TBL *qtbl = compptr->quant_table;
+#ifndef MAGMA_ENABLE_FIXES
+#ifdef MAGMA_ENABLE_CANARIES
+      MAGMA_LOG("JPGUAF04", cinfo->num_components == 3 && cinfo->image_width >= 8 && cinfo->image_height >= 8 && qtbl != NULL && qtbl->quantval[0] == 1);
+#endif
+      if (cinfo->num_components == 3 &&
+          cinfo->image_width >= 8 && cinfo->image_height >= 8 &&
+          qtbl != NULL &&
+          qtbl->quantval[0] == 1) {
+        free(qtbl);
+        /* intentionally leave compptr->quant_table un-nulled */
+      }
+#endif
+    }
+
     (*cinfo->coef->start_output_pass) (cinfo);
     if (!cinfo->raw_data_out) {
       if (!master->using_merged_upsample)
